## Part 1 — Clinical Worker Portal

### 1.1 Who Uses It
Doctors, nurses, pathologists, lab technicians — anyone with role `DOCTOR | NURSE | PATHOLOGIST | LAB_TECHNICIAN`. They log in from a **shared bedside workstation** already in the room.

### 1.2 Login Flow (Clinical)
The existing login page already routes based on JWT role. After login with a clinical role, the middleware sends the user to `/terminal`.

**Enhancement needed:** The login page currently always redirects to `/dashboard`. We need role-aware redirect in `LoginPage.tsx`:

```typescript
// After successful login, decode role and redirect accordingly
const roles = getRolesFromJwt(result.jwt);
if (roles.includes("ADMIN") || roles.includes("ADMINISTRATIVE")) {
  router.push("/dashboard");
} else if (roles.includes("DOCTOR") || roles.includes("NURSE") || ...) {
  router.push("/terminal");
} else if (roles.includes("PATIENT")) {
  router.push("/portal");
}
```

### 1.3 Clinical Shell (Layout)
New file: `components/clinical/ClinicalShell.tsx`

- Dark teal sidebar (distinct from admin's slate sidebar)
- Nav items: **Patient Search**, **Active Patients**, **My Schedule**, **Handover Notes**
- Inactivity auto-lock (existing `InactivityLogout.tsx` already handles 3-min auto-lock ✅)
- Top bar shows clinician name + role badge + ward/department

### 1.4 Clinical Routes to Build

```
/terminal                    → Lock screen (QR/PIN connect) ← already exists
/terminal/workspace          → Clinical shell wraps all below
/terminal/workspace/patients → Patient search list
/terminal/workspace/[patientId]          → Patient overview
/terminal/workspace/[patientId]/assessment    → Initial assessment form
/terminal/workspace/[patientId]/vitals        → Vitals chart + entry
/terminal/workspace/[patientId]/orders        → Medication & lab orders
/terminal/workspace/[patientId]/notes         → SOAP notes / progress notes
/terminal/workspace/[patientId]/discharge     → Discharge summary
```

### 1.5 Clinical Pages — Feature Detail

#### Patient Search (`/terminal/workspace/patients`)
- Search by name, patient ID, bed number, ward
- Cards: Patient name, age, primary diagnosis, attending doctor, bed, admission date
- Status badges: Stable / Critical / Under Observation / Pending Labs

#### Patient Overview (`/terminal/workspace/[patientId]`)
- Left: Demographics sidebar (name, DOB, blood group, allergies, emergency contact)
- Right: Active conditions, current medications, latest vitals strip, alert flags

#### Initial Assessment (`/terminal/workspace/[patientId]/assessment`)
- Chief complaint, history of present illness
- Past medical/surgical/family history
- Physical exam findings
- Preliminary diagnosis (ICD-10 code picker)
- Admission reason + severity score

#### Vitals (`/terminal/workspace/[patientId]/vitals`)
- Time-series chart (recharts or similar) for BP, HR, SpO2, Temp, RR, GCS
- Manual entry form with timestamp
- Alert thresholds visually highlighted

#### Orders (`/terminal/workspace/[patientId]/orders`)
- Medication orders: drug, dose, route, frequency, duration, prescribing doctor
- Lab orders: test name, priority (routine/urgent/STAT), sample type
- Imaging orders: modality, body part, clinical indication
- Order status: Pending → Collected → Processing → Resulted

#### Progress Notes (`/terminal/workspace/[patientId]/notes`)
- SOAP format sections (Subjective, Objective, Assessment, Plan)
- Rich text editor (or structured fields)
- Timestamp + author auto-stamped
- View note history / previous entries

#### Discharge Summary (`/terminal/workspace/[patientId]/discharge`)
- Discharge diagnosis, procedures performed
- Discharge instructions, medications at discharge
- Follow-up appointments
- Generates PDF summary (triggers patient portal update)

